{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>A different spirit.</b> Two spirits — one in the mouth and one in the heart. To the spies he said, 'I am with you in counsel,' but in his heart he intended to speak the truth. Therefore he had the strength to silence them, as it says (Numbers 13), ״וַיַּהַס כָלֵב״ — for they assumed he would speak as they did. This is what is said concerning Caleb son of Jephunneh: ״וָאָשֵׁב אֹתוֹ דָבָר כַּאֲשֶׁר עִם לְבָבִי״ (Joshua 14) — and not as was with my mouth (Tanḥuma)." "<b>And he was filled after.</b> He filled his heart after Me — and this is an elliptical verse." "<b>Who came there.</b> Hebron shall be given to him." "<b>He shall possess it.</b> As the Targum renders: ״יְתַרְכֻנַּהּ״ — they shall dispossess the Anakim and the people who are in it. And one should not render it ״יַרְתִּינַהּ״ except where it says ״יִירָשֶׁנָּה״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Rashi writes בְּסֵ' as an abbreviation for בְּסֵפֶר, 'in the book of'; resolved as 'concerning Caleb son of Jephunneh' from context."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:57.145656671Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}